  "source": "Vanilla ElytraModel.createLayer (1.21.8), feet-at-origin geometry only: left_wing addBox(-10,0,0,10,20,2) at PartPose.offset(5,0,0), right_wing addBox(0,0,0,10,20,2).mirror() at (-5,0,0), both CubeDeformation(1) texOffs(22,0) on a 64x32 texture. Java y runs down from the shoulder, so Bedrock y = 24 - java y. The pose rotations (standing/crouching/gliding, from PlayerElytraAnimationState) are applied at runtime through boneMatrices' `extra`, not baked here; the crouching pose alone moves the wings down 3 px and uses elytra_wings_crouch.geo.json."
